.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt IFCONFIG 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ifconfig
.Nd configure and inspect network interfaces
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Ar interface
.Nm
.Ar interface
.Ar address Ns Op / Ns Ar prefix
.Nm
.Ar interface
.Cm up | down
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
lists the interfaces registered by the
.Dq net:
server. With one interface name it prints that interface's address, netmask, flags and MTU.
The address form sets the IPv4 address and prefix length through
.Dv SET_ADDRESS ; the default prefix is 24. The
.Cm up
and
.Cm down
forms change the administrative state through
.Dv SET_STATE .
.Pp
Only the native
.Dq net:
control API is used; there is no ioctl or privileged path. Unknown interfaces, malformed
addresses and prefixes outside
.Dv 0..=32
are errors and the tool exits non-zero.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nc 8 ,
.Xr netd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
